      "message": "LGTM (based on opus 4.8 analysis)\n\n  Verdict: effective and correct — fully resolves issue #715.\n\n  - The bug is real. search_results(search) (wiki.py:99) and available_hosts(search) (wiki.py:106) each take a required positional search, but their\n    route decorators supply no URL converter. A direct GET calls them with no argument → TypeError → 500. Matches the issue.\n  - The fix is the right one. Both are only ever called in-process: /available\u0027s POST handler calls search_results(), which calls available_hosts().\n    Dropping the decorators (the issue\u0027s recommended option) removes the broken endpoints while preserving the working /available flow.\n  - No collateral breakage (verified): no url_for to these endpoints, no JS/template hits /results or /available_hosts (the page\u0027s only AJAX call\n    goes to /api/v3/disks/types), and no tests reference them.\n  - The 3 deleted templates are genuinely dead: not included/imported anywhere; nav is now rendered by bootstrap_render.py. They\u0027re leftovers from\n    the wiki→quads-web migration (commit e642b43). The only other hit is auto-generated egg-info/SOURCES.txt.\n  - No coverage impact: quads.web isn\u0027t in the tox coverage scope.",
